---
source: crates/modde-cli/tests/cli_help_snapshots.rs
expression: "stdout(&[\"game\", \"add\", \"--help\"])"
---
Add or overwrite a user-defined game registration

Usage: modde game add [OPTIONS] --display-name <DISPLAY_NAME> --executable-dir <EXECUTABLE_DIR> <ID>

Arguments:
  <ID>  

Options:
      --data-dir <DATA_DIR>
          Override data directory (default: ~/.local/share/modde or $`MODDE_DATA_DIR`) [env: MODDE_DATA_DIR=]
      --display-name <DISPLAY_NAME>
          
      --config-dir <CONFIG_DIR>
          Override the base configuration directory used by modde and its session journal
      --executable-dir <EXECUTABLE_DIR>
          
      --heap-profile <HEAP_PROFILE>
          Write a DHAT heap profile. Requires the `heap-profile` cargo feature [env: MODDE_HEAP_PROFILE=]
      --steam-app-id <STEAM_APP_ID>
          
      --install-dir-name <INSTALL_DIR_NAME>
          
      --mod-dir <MOD_DIR>
          
      --nexus-domain <NEXUS_DOMAIN>
          
      --proxy-dll <PROXY_DLLS>
          
      --force
          Overwrite an existing user-defined game TOML
  -h, --help
          Print help
